To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\blueD{\text{multiply it by } \dfrac{1}{3}} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{12}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD {y} &=\greenD{12} \blueD{\times \dfrac{1}{3}} \\\\
\maroonD {y}&=\maroonD{4}
\end{align}$
